Everything outside godbot/ and modules/godbot-native/ started as that directory.
Files changed for Godbot say "Modified for Godbot" at the top, or mark the changed
parts with "Godbot:". The changes:

  - Android only: the iOS archive script, the ios/ios:archive scripts, the iOS block
    of app.json and the iOS build settings of app.config.js are removed.
  - Name, scheme (godbot://), Android package (io.github.renjiegod.godbot), storage
    keys (godbot.*), demo flag (EXPO_PUBLIC_GODBOT_DEMO), signing variables
    (GODBOT_ANDROID_*). The version comes from this app's own package.json.
  - Shared code comes from Godbot (godbot/, below) instead of ds-bot/src/client,
    ds-bot/src/shared and link/src, so the app draws Godbot's main Bot and themes.
  - The handshake names the API versions the app speaks and checks the computer's
    plugin; an incompatible computer is retried with a growing delay and an upgrade
    hint, and DS Bot on the other end is named.
  - A pairing link opened from outside the app asks for confirmation (computer name
    and Server) before anything is sent. Both godbot:// and dsbot:// links pair.
  - The Updates page shows Godbot's update phases and its update mode.
  - Errors from the computer that the app cannot translate show exactly as they came.
  - Bot browsers that Godbot runs in its own environments get a clear message.
  - Side chat reads state incrementally instead of the whole state every 1.5 s.
  - Forgetting a computer also forgets its push key.
  - New: end-to-end encrypted push (src/team/push-*.ts, fcm.ts, notify.ts),
    "Keep connected in background" (src/team/keepalive.ts and the native module),
    background notifications for notices, and in-app updates of this app
    (src/team/app-update*.ts).
  - New config plugins: plugins/network-security.js (cleartext only to localhost,
    127.0.0.1 and 10.0.2.2) and plugins/fcm.js (Firebase only when
    GODBOT_GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON names a google-services.json).

